# ============================================================
# Frontend environment — usually NOT needed
# ============================================================
# The React app normally needs NO .env file at all.
#
# Default behaviour (leave everything unset):
#   - src/api/client.ts sets API_BASE = '' (empty)
#   - requests go to relative paths: /api/v1/...
#   - the Vite dev server proxies /api to the backend
#     (see vite.config.ts -> BACKEND_PROXY_TARGET)
#   - Docker Compose sets BACKEND_PROXY_TARGET=http://backend:3001
#   - local dev without Docker falls back to http://localhost:3001
#
# Only set VITE_API_URL if the API is served from a DIFFERENT origin than the
# frontend (e.g. a production static bundle on its own domain). When you do,
# remember to set CORS_ORIGIN on the backend to the frontend's exact origin.
#
# Example:
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# Note: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the bundle, and it
# inlines them at BUILD time — changing this requires rebuilding the frontend.
